(3690323, 517604, 39144, '<td valign="top">Definitely an interesting hairdo. I really like the detail, contrast and coloring of this image. I''m not a big fan of the crop. The shoulder/back of the second person is a bit distracting.</td>', 'Definitely an interesting hairdo. I really like the detail, contrast and coloring of this image. I''m not a big fan of the crop. The shoulder/back of the second person is a bit distracting.', '2007-05-24 10:46:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(3690328, 518442, 39144, '<td valign="top">This is a nice image and composition, but there does not seem to be anything too white. The lightes shade I can see is kind of a muddied up white, maybe 20% grey. I would like to see brighter whites in this image too.</td>', 'This is a nice image and composition, but there does not seem to be anything too white. The lightes shade I can see is kind of a muddied up white, maybe 20% grey. I would like to see brighter whites in this image too.', '2007-05-24 10:47:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(3690337, 518839, 39144, '<td valign="top">This is a very interesting subject to look at. Unfortunately, the DOF looks just a bit too shallow (the top fin appears a bit out of the focus range) and the lighting is a bit strange. A subject like this would probably benefit from a bit more controlled lighting situation to minimize/prevent the distracting reflections and glare in the dolphin.</td>', 'This is a very interesting subject to look at. Unfortunately, the DOF looks just a bit too shallow (the top fin appears a bit out of the focus range) and the lighting is a bit strange. A subject like this would probably benefit from a bit more controlled lighting situation to minimize/prevent the distracting reflections and glare in the dolphin.', '2007-05-24 10:49:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3690345, 518980, 39144, '<td valign="top">One of the best images in this challenge for sure. Excellent work. The centered composition really works well to achieve a balance photo, and the use of these particular glasses with the crooked stem keep the photo from looking too plain. Definitely a top 10 image.</td>', 'One of the best images in this challenge for sure. Excellent work. The centered composition really works well to achieve a balance photo, and the use of these particular glasses with the crooked stem keep the photo from looking too plain. Definitely a top 10 image.', '2007-05-24 10:51:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(3690358, 514631, 39144, '<td valign="top">Very cute image and+ lighting. The dedicated look on her face to get the cupcake open is great. I do wish you made use of the full 640 pixels though. And I''m sorry, but I do have to comment about the date on the photo. Having your camera print the date on your photo can completely destroy a good photo. It did in the film days too, but it was necessary for those who wanted to keep track of when they took the picture. Now, in the digital age, that and much more is stored in the EXIF infor of 99% of the digital cameras out there, thus eliminating the need to have it ruining the photo. I would definitely recommend removing that option from the camera for the challenge photos, and really for all photos that you take. It''s just not worth it to ruin such a good photo with something that you can''t remove. You can always add it as a layer in photoshop if you want, but then it can be removed too. Just my .02.</td>', 'Very cute image and+ lighting. The dedicated look on her face to get the cupcake open is great. I do wish you made use of the full 640 pixels though. And I''m sorry, but I do have to comment about the date on the photo. Having your camera print the date on your photo can completely destroy a good photo. It did in the film days too, but it was necessary for those who wanted to keep track of when they took the picture. Now, in the digital age, that and much more is stored in the EXIF infor of 99% of the digital cameras out there, thus eliminating the need to have it ruining the photo. I would definitely recommend removing that option from the camera for the challenge photos, and really for all photos that you take. It''s just not worth it to ruin such a good photo with something that you can''t remove. You can always add it as a layer in photoshop if you want, but then it can be removed too. Just my .02.', '2007-05-24 10:55:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3690388, 518376, 20018, '<td valign="top">interesting subject but with the distracting background and harsh lighting, it''s an unremarkable shot.  If you can''t get a better background , and you have access to it, you might try and take a shot at night with (at minimum) two diffuse lighting sources.  (One light possibly sharp) and keep light off the fence if possible.</td>', 'interesting subject but with the distracting background and harsh lighting, it''s an unremarkable shot.  If you can''t get a better background , and you have access to it, you might try and take a shot at night with (at minimum) two diffuse lighting sources.  (One light possibly sharp) and keep light off the fence if possible.', '2007-05-24 11:07:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(3690393, 518449, 20018, '<td valign="top">nice composition/lighting. I enjoy the natural movement, balance, and dynamic repetition.</td>', 'nice composition/lighting. I enjoy the natural movement, balance, and dynamic repetition.', '2007-05-24 11:09:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3690419, 514634, 20018, '<td valign="top">seriously, less clothing or more uniform clothing, as well as, better choice of pose could''ve helped this shot tremendously, and the model would be perfect for it (too much eyeliner though). If you started with the idea of an hourglass, I''d recommend focusing more on it than including all the excess elements.  Emphasis is taken away by the cleavage, hand pose, face, and stool. nice lighting and background relationship/use. Overall: nice image of the model but  as a challenge entry it seems more like the an afterthought.</td>', 'seriously, less clothing or more uniform clothing, as well as, better choice of pose could''ve helped this shot tremendously, and the model would be perfect for it (too much eyeliner though). If you started with the idea of an hourglass, I''d recommend focusing more on it than including all the excess elements.  Emphasis is taken away by the cleavage, hand pose, face, and stool. nice lighting and background relationship/use. Overall: nice image of the model but  as a challenge entry it seems more like the an afterthought.', '2007-05-24 11:17:28.000000', NULL, 1),
