(3713887, 517823, 30049, '<td valign="top">From photographer''s comments:<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MelonMusketeer:</b></div><hr/><i>I put the original at the top of my portfolio for the week or so, as I don''t know how to post a link here.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Here you go Waddy.  :)<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=524247" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/69008/thumb/524247.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/69008/thumb/524247.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/69008/thumb/524247.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>BTW - To add an image to your Photograher Comments area just click on the challenge entry photo from your profile page, the use the ''edit details'' (or something like that) link that is visible in the Photograph Information area.  Use {thumb}image#{/thumb} to insert the desired photo thumbnail (replace the { } braces with [ ] brackets).<br/> <br/>Looks like you avoided the rule of thirds police just fine...now to combat the should have centered it group.  :P</td>', 'From photographer''s comments: Originally posted by MelonMusketeer:I put the original at the top of my portfolio for the week or so, as I don''t know how to post a link here. Here you go Waddy.  :)   BTW - To add an image to your Photograher Comments area just click on the challenge entry photo from your profile page, the use the ''edit details'' (or something like that) link that is visible in the Photograph Information area.  Use {thumb}image#{/thumb} to insert the desired photo thumbnail (replace the { } braces with [ ] brackets). Looks like you avoided the rule of thirds police just fine...now to combat the should have centered it group.  :P', '2007-05-30 11:07:42.000000', NULL, 0),
