(3717679, 517669, 76335, '<td valign="top">Sometimes you can be so close to something that you can''t see it for what it is (or what it looks like, which is all that really matters). I never thought of this shot as blurry or out of focus, and I''m not sure it is. But I think it _looks_ that way. This is actually a reflection of the building from the rear window of a car. Car windows, I''m learning, don''t make for the best reflective surfaces -- at least this one didn''t. It almost looks doubly reflected in some places, like the glass might be layered. I kind of looked past that when I took this through post-processing. All the same, I''m happy this finished above five; it was a fun experiment.</td>', 'Sometimes you can be so close to something that you can''t see it for what it is (or what it looks like, which is all that really matters). I never thought of this shot as blurry or out of focus, and I''m not sure it is. But I think it _looks_ that way. This is actually a reflection of the building from the rear window of a car. Car windows, I''m learning, don''t make for the best reflective surfaces -- at least this one didn''t. It almost looks doubly reflected in some places, like the glass might be layered. I kind of looked past that when I took this through post-processing. All the same, I''m happy this finished above five; it was a fun experiment.', '2007-05-30 23:26:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3717704, 517878, 67697, '<td valign="top">The sky and clouds are amazing.  I love the silhouette.  Congrats on the top 10!</td>', 'The sky and clouds are amazing.  I love the silhouette.  Congrats on the top 10!', '2007-05-30 23:33:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3717896, 514188, 63398, '<td valign="top">Just wonderful, Jeff! You really nailed it in this shot. I really like the way that the railing, which normally would be curving back on itself gives the illusion of many different ones fanned out. Perfect angle IMNSHO. Congrats on your first ribbon!</td>', 'Just wonderful, Jeff! You really nailed it in this shot. I really like the way that the railing, which normally would be curving back on itself gives the illusion of many different ones fanned out. Perfect angle IMNSHO. Congrats on your first ribbon!', '2007-05-31 00:27:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718099, 515929, 18197, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club. <br/> <br/>Looking at your photo, I see an interesting shape. Foreground/background dynamics are interesting. I''m a blue fan, so the colors resonate with me. I can see this as a background image in an advertisement.<br/> <br/>But it doesn''t hold my interest, and is less interesting than other subjects in the challenge. It is one thing to master your camera and the post processing and another to take photos that engage your audience. You have very good performance on the former, but could work on the latter.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.  Looking at your photo, I see an interesting shape. Foreground/background dynamics are interesting. I''m a blue fan, so the colors resonate with me. I can see this as a background image in an advertisement. But it doesn''t hold my interest, and is less interesting than other subjects in the challenge. It is one thing to master your camera and the post processing and another to take photos that engage your audience. You have very good performance on the former, but could work on the latter.', '2007-05-31 01:15:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718105, 514188, 68239, '<td valign="top">Dramatic lines really pop. Excellent imo. Good work.</td>', 'Dramatic lines really pop. Excellent imo. Good work.', '2007-05-31 01:17:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718550, 514188, 72700, '<td valign="top">Exellent shot!!!!!!</td>', 'Exellent shot!!!!!!', '2007-05-31 07:28:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718684, 515619, 66597, '<td valign="top">Julianne, I also thought of Sandy P''s photo when voting on this, and think you did an outstanding job with this! I love the curve in his beak, and you captured his blue eye nicely.</td>', 'Julianne, I also thought of Sandy P''s photo when voting on this, and think you did an outstanding job with this! I love the curve in his beak, and you captured his blue eye nicely.', '2007-05-31 09:04:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718688, 517022, 66597, '<td valign="top">Nice concept here, especially with the bands on the rose petal. I think the only way you could get this in totally sharp focus and not blow out all the reflections from the bands would be to take it in a light tent. I also think it would be interesting to see it with the whole rose petal.</td>', 'Nice concept here, especially with the bands on the rose petal. I think the only way you could get this in totally sharp focus and not blow out all the reflections from the bands would be to take it in a light tent. I also think it would be interesting to see it with the whole rose petal.', '2007-05-31 09:06:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718695, 513688, 66597, '<td valign="top">I like the textures and concept of this a lot. What hurt you, I think, is the lighting and composition, but you probably already know that, as we''ve seen some beautiful work from you :-) A warming filter and some added brightness to pop the textures would be coool here.</td>', 'I like the textures and concept of this a lot. What hurt you, I think, is the lighting and composition, but you probably already know that, as we''ve seen some beautiful work from you :-) A warming filter and some added brightness to pop the textures would be coool here.', '2007-05-31 09:11:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718706, 514627, 66597, '<td valign="top">Lea, this is very cute. The even lighting and composition are very strong here. The skin tones look a little washed out on my monitor. I think the thing that probably really hurt you scorewise was the primary bubble right under his chin - if it were in sharp focus and the tones in the photo just a little richer, this would be a potential ribbon winner. I think this would be a great addition to your portfolio if you cloned the big bubble out altogether (realize you couldn''t do that for the challenge, of course.) You really are very, very strong with portraits.</td>', 'Lea, this is very cute. The even lighting and composition are very strong here. The skin tones look a little washed out on my monitor. I think the thing that probably really hurt you scorewise was the primary bubble right under his chin - if it were in sharp focus and the tones in the photo just a little richer, this would be a potential ribbon winner. I think this would be a great addition to your portfolio if you cloned the big bubble out altogether (realize you couldn''t do that for the challenge, of course.) You really are very, very strong with portraits.', '2007-05-31 09:17:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718709, 518495, 66597, '<td valign="top">A most interesting photo, one that I kept coming back to in the shapes challenge. I think the lighting and textures are very, very well done. The shadow across the top probably took a point off your score - DPC voters are very picky. Mostly I will say "very well seen." A photo I wish I had taken.</td>', 'A most interesting photo, one that I kept coming back to in the shapes challenge. I think the lighting and textures are very, very well done. The shadow across the top probably took a point off your score - DPC voters are very picky. Mostly I will say "very well seen." A photo I wish I had taken.', '2007-05-31 09:19:54.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(3718716, 517845, 66597, '<td valign="top">Jackal, there are some real strengths in this photo - I remember thinking the luminosity of those chess pieces had a lot of potential when I voted on it. The DOF is great, as are the lines. What I think would be very cool would be to shoot this on a light table (just some lights under a piece of glass supported by a pair of sawhorses would work fine) so that the light is absorbed up through these beautiful pieces. Of course, that might not work with the chess board - don''t know what it is made of.</td>', 'Jackal, there are some real strengths in this photo - I remember thinking the luminosity of those chess pieces had a lot of potential when I voted on it. The DOF is great, as are the lines. What I think would be very cool would be to shoot this on a light table (just some lights under a piece of glass supported by a pair of sawhorses would work fine) so that the light is absorbed up through these beautiful pieces. Of course, that might not work with the chess board - don''t know what it is made of.', '2007-05-31 09:22:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718722, 518476, 66597, '<td valign="top">I like the concept, textures and lighting a lot! I wish that black cork were just a wee bit further down - maybe swapped out with the Vintner''s collection cork - think that would strengthen the composition. Great entry for shapes!</td>', 'I like the concept, textures and lighting a lot! I wish that black cork were just a wee bit further down - maybe swapped out with the Vintner''s collection cork - think that would strengthen the composition. Great entry for shapes!', '2007-05-31 09:27:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718781, 517499, 15266, '<td valign="top">Congrats on that first blue, Robert!   Its a fantastic image for the topic.  :D</td>', 'Congrats on that first blue, Robert!   Its a fantastic image for the topic.  :D', '2007-05-31 09:59:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718800, 517891, 35004, '<td valign="top">I really like it. I don''t know why, I just do!</td>', 'I really like it. I don''t know why, I just do!', '2007-05-31 10:06:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718976, 518255, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Yes, the British have some fabulous museums in London, don''t they.  (I usually head for the Nat''l Gallery and the Tate)<br/> <br/>You''ve captured a remarkable juxtaposition of eras, shapes and tones in one image.  Still, your composition is quiet enough so that the viewer is not confused by all the information.  That''s probably why you scored so well in this difficult Challenge.  <br/> <br/>So, I''ll say "congratulations" on a fine image and I''m delighted to have had the chance to view it again.<br/> <br/>SFAlice</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Yes, the British have some fabulous museums in London, don''t they.  (I usually head for the Nat''l Gallery and the Tate) You''ve captured a remarkable juxtaposition of eras, shapes and tones in one image.  Still, your composition is quiet enough so that the viewer is not confused by all the information.  That''s probably why you scored so well in this difficult Challenge.   So, I''ll say "congratulations" on a fine image and I''m delighted to have had the chance to view it again. SFAlice', '2007-05-31 11:26:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3718991, 515619, 51597, '<td valign="top">Wow!!  Perfect for shapes. The blue eye stands out. the whole picture stands out..</td>', 'Wow!!  Perfect for shapes. The blue eye stands out. the whole picture stands out..', '2007-05-31 11:30:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719015, 517878, 62318, '<td valign="top">Very nice silhouette and a beautiful cloud formation. Great score. I''m glad it did so well for you. It almost looks like something from a book.</td>', 'Very nice silhouette and a beautiful cloud formation. Great score. I''m glad it did so well for you. It almost looks like something from a book.', '2007-05-31 11:41:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719023, 514627, 62318, '<td valign="top">Going for a high key shot? Not bad, I disagree with the amount of light. I think it is fine. I might have moved the little one a bit further from the way to prevent shadow casting but that is pretty minor. For "shapes" though it is a bit hard to see the bubbles and probably would have scored higher with more emphasis on them. Cute picture though. Very inquisitive face!</td>', 'Going for a high key shot? Not bad, I disagree with the amount of light. I think it is fine. I might have moved the little one a bit further from the way to prevent shadow casting but that is pretty minor. For "shapes" though it is a bit hard to see the bubbles and probably would have scored higher with more emphasis on them. Cute picture though. Very inquisitive face!', '2007-05-31 11:44:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719031, 515619, 62318, '<td valign="top">Terrific shot Julie. I think this is a wonderful take on the challenge. The shape is so subtle but yet very pronounced at the same time. Great detail and wonderful colors. congrats on the terrific image.</td>', 'Terrific shot Julie. I think this is a wonderful take on the challenge. The shape is so subtle but yet very pronounced at the same time. Great detail and wonderful colors. congrats on the terrific image.', '2007-05-31 11:45:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719108, 518304, 5885, '<td valign="top">It''s not bad. From the votes it got it looks like voters thought it was quite average. <br/> <br/>Technicals are good, although I think completely darkened silhouette for the face would have been stronger. <br/> <br/>Compositionally, it would have been strengthened by cropping of the black corner off the edge of the umbrella and the white behind the neck. Both are distracting to the eye. <br/> <br/>Subject matter, and this only my opinion, is rather boring. No pop, no wow. And that''s what it takes to get high scores at DPC.<br/> <br/>All this adds up to a rather average score. Anyway, I hope that helps. Hope to see more soon.</td>', 'It''s not bad. From the votes it got it looks like voters thought it was quite average.  Technicals are good, although I think completely darkened silhouette for the face would have been stronger.  Compositionally, it would have been strengthened by cropping of the black corner off the edge of the umbrella and the white behind the neck. Both are distracting to the eye.  Subject matter, and this only my opinion, is rather boring. No pop, no wow. And that''s what it takes to get high scores at DPC. All this adds up to a rather average score. Anyway, I hope that helps. Hope to see more soon.', '2007-05-31 12:12:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719132, 518304, 61559, '<td valign="top">Challenge Performance: There''s one human image in the top 20 and then the next is at 56th. There are very few people shots in the Challenge. The majority must have believed that finding interesting shapes in nature or architecture, etc. was what the Challenge was about. Not portraiture.<br/> <br/>I like the way the lines of the umbrella lead into his face and I like his "thoughtful" expression. <br/> <br/>I''m not sure how I would have voted on it though. Something really has to grab me to get high marks and I don''t think that would have happened as I was browsing through the entries.</td>', 'Challenge Performance: There''s one human image in the top 20 and then the next is at 56th. There are very few people shots in the Challenge. The majority must have believed that finding interesting shapes in nature or architecture, etc. was what the Challenge was about. Not portraiture. I like the way the lines of the umbrella lead into his face and I like his "thoughtful" expression.  I''m not sure how I would have voted on it though. Something really has to grab me to get high marks and I don''t think that would have happened as I was browsing through the entries.', '2007-05-31 12:25:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719154, 518304, 43031, '<td valign="top">TO do this shot right, put up a white background and point the light at that. The umbrella showing is just cheesy. <br/> <br/>For the idea of Faith (I assume you wanted to make the "shape of prayer/faith" ?? ) you should have had the traditional hands in praying position shot. Something like the following, I presume.<br/> <br/>//www.istockphoto.com/file_closeup/?id=3042513&amp;refnum=708451&amp;Lang=en<br/> <br/>ALso, a good idea, google/flickr the subject or description of your idea. Sometimes it can give you inspiration. Don''t be afraid to make an exact copy of the original (no, I don''t mean copy/past :P ) while you are learning. It can teach you a lot about how to light things, and the minutiae of photo setups. some on flickr.com will post their setups also. If you haven''t yet, check out strobist.com, and go throught the Lighting 101 course on the side there.</td>', 'TO do this shot right, put up a white background and point the light at that. The umbrella showing is just cheesy.  For the idea of Faith (I assume you wanted to make the "shape of prayer/faith" ?? ) you should have had the traditional hands in praying position shot. Something like the following, I presume. //www.istockphoto.com/file_closeup/?id=3042513&refnum=708451&Lang=en ALso, a good idea, google/flickr the subject or description of your idea. Sometimes it can give you inspiration. Don''t be afraid to make an exact copy of the original (no, I don''t mean copy/past :P ) while you are learning. It can teach you a lot about how to light things, and the minutiae of photo setups. some on flickr.com will post their setups also. If you haven''t yet, check out strobist.com, and go throught the Lighting 101 course on the side there.', '2007-05-31 12:36:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719200, 515198, 61651, '<td valign="top">What an interesting image - great take on the challenge!  I agree with posthumous - size it a bit bigger for greater impact on your voters.</td>', 'What an interesting image - great take on the challenge!  I agree with posthumous - size it a bit bigger for greater impact on your voters.', '2007-05-31 12:56:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719412, 517499, 65025, '<td valign="top">This is such a great shot!</td>', 'This is such a great shot!', '2007-05-31 14:35:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719826, 518196, 26255, '<td valign="top">Seriously underrated!</td>', 'Seriously underrated!', '2007-05-31 16:17:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3719858, 518196, 19708, '<td valign="top">gotta'' love the title.<br/>:)</td>', 'gotta'' love the title.:)', '2007-05-31 16:28:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3720617, 514634, 72131, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t like the hokey studio lighting but the crop is very good. It''s the kind of crop you learn in art school to emphasize shape and negative space. You got a low score because DPC voters know nothing about composition. Less than nothing. They know all the wrong things. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks =]</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: I don''t like the hokey studio lighting but the crop is very good. It''s the kind of crop you learn in art school to emphasize shape and negative space. You got a low score because DPC voters know nothing about composition. Less than nothing. They know all the wrong things.   thanks =]', '2007-05-31 20:34:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3721075, 517499, 33362, '<td valign="top">Great shot Robert. Congratulations on the blue!!!<br/>Nick</td>', 'Great shot Robert. Congratulations on the blue!!!Nick', '2007-05-31 22:52:38.000000', NULL, 0),
